# Integrality over ℂ[j⁻¹] bounds growth at every cusp

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.eventually_norm_slash_le_mul_of_isIntegral_adjoin_jqModC_inv_sq`
(`9bd551e6-c3d5-55c4-b5e6-c3743e9d8521`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `f8a47d3c-423e-51a9-aabe-9dca7b583439`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ containing the translation
matrix $T$, let $k\in\mathbb{Z}$, and let $m\ge 1$ be a natural number. Let $g,h$ be modular forms
of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, with $h\ne 0$, and let $X$
be a Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}$ satisfying $X\cdot \mathrm{qExp}(h)=\mathrm{qExp}(g)$, where
$\mathrm{qExp}(\cdot)$ denotes the $q$-expansion of width $1$ viewed in $\mathbb{C}((q))$. Write
$\bar j=$ `jqModC ℂ`, the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ of the
integral power series `jNum` $=$ `eisenstein4`$^3\cdot$`dedekindEtaUnitInv`. Assume that $X^2\,\bar
j^{\,m}\,(\bar j-1728)^m$ is integral over the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}((q))$
generated by $\bar j^{-1}$. Then for every $A\in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ there is a real constant
$C$ such that, for $\tau$ in the upper half plane eventually along the filter at $i\infty$,
$$\bigl\|\bigl((z\mapsto g(z)(E_4(z)^2E_6(z))^m)\mid_{k+14m}A\bigr)(\tau)\bigr\|\le
C\,\bigl\|\bigl((z\mapsto h(z)\Delta(z)^m)\mid_{k+12m}A\bigr)(\tau)\bigr\|,$$
the slash being taken for the image of $A$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$.

This is the level-generic growth estimate transporting integrality of a quotient of $q$-expansions
over $\mathbb{C}[j^{-1}]$ into a bound at an arbitrary cusp, the cusp being reached by the slash
action of $A\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and $j^{-1}$ tending to $0$ there. It is used in the
construction of a modular form on $\Gamma_1$ whose $q$-expansion is a prescribed multiple of a power
of a theta series, in
[`ModularCurve.exists_modularForm_gamma1_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_modularForm_gamma1_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral).

